First of all, how can you "be careful" when sitting on a throne?  I've
had little success with thrones, so I'd appreciate any hints here.  The
worst thing that ever happened to me when I sat on a throne was the room
filled with critters, several of whom were dragons with a bead already
drawn on me (I never got a move in).

On part (b), this is a magic trap, not a monster trap, although it might
seem like a monster trap from the most frequent results of tripping them ;^).

I really like these traps once I have ESP and a blindfold.  The only
drawback is when you loose permanent hitpoints (which there is a remedy
for - those cursed scrolls of genocide come in handy here).  It's been a
while, so I can't remember which result of the trap it is that makes you
loose permanent hitpoints.  But I remember that after a while you gain
either an intrinsice or an artifact of some kind that protects you from
this result (I must be a geaser - I've forgotten more about this game than
I knew about it when I started reading this group).  ;^)

Someone want to refresh my memory, and add any hints about the thrones?

Really, I consider magic traps to be one of the best and safest ways to
gain experience/corpses/food/items quickly.  Just make sure you're
telepathic at the least...

